==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|purveu||proviso}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|purveuest||it is provided}}, or {{m|fro|purveu que||provided that}} (statutory language), from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|porveu||provided}}, past participle of {{m|fro|porveoir||to provide}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|prōvideō}} (See [[provide]]). Influenced by {{m|en|view}} and its etymological antecedants.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[enact]]ing part of a [[statute]].
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[scope]] of a statute.
# Scope or [[range]] of interest or [[control]].
#* {{quote-book|chapter=The Right of the Convention to Frame such a Constitution|title=[[w:The Federalist|The Federalist]]: A Commentary on the Constitution of the United States|page=255|year=1788|author=[[w:James Madison|James Madison]]|passage=Will it be said that the fundamental principles of the Confederation were not within the '''purview''' of the convention, and ought not to have been varied?}}
#* {{quote-book|year=2003|title=Logics of Conversation|page=7|author=Nicholas Asher and Alex Lascarides|passage=Rhetorical relations have truth conditional effects that contribute to meaning but lie outside the '''purview''' of compositional semantics.}}
# [[range|Range]] of understanding.
{{rfex|en}}

